Subject: [PATCH] DeepCrack eval script, ruff/mypy pass, speed metrics, and a
 real bug fix

scripts/eval_deepcrack.py (NEW): the missing piece flagged after the last
status check - DeepCrack was held out for OOD zero-shot eval since Phase
1b, but nothing ever queried a trained checkpoint against it. Reuses the
checkpoint's LEARNED context tokens throughout (including for the negative
control), since CoOp's premise is that a learned context generalises to
new class names - the same premise demo.py relies on for live queries.
Reports per-tier AP plus an absurd-prompt control, and carries Phase 1b's
measured box-looseness caveat (median fill ratio 16.6%) into the printed
output itself, not just the docs. Verified end to end against a synthetic
placeholder dataset (no real DeepCrack data available) and a real trained
checkpoint - found and fixed one real display bug in the process:
DetectionValidator prints model.names for its per-class table, which was
still whatever NEU-DET's class 0 was ("crazing") rather than the actual
DeepCrack query, since matching is by index and never needed the string -
now overridden per-query so the printed label is honest.

ruff + mypy pass across src/tgfem/ and the scripts I've written (Phases
4-8) - not the pre-existing Phase 0-3 files, left alone deliberately.
Fixed: dead unused variables, f-strings without placeholders, dict()
calls rewritten as literals, an explicit check=False on a subprocess.run
whose return code is checked manually, next() instead of building a whole
list for one element. mypy needed real type annotations (not just
suppression) on TextEncoder's CLIP sub-module attributes and
ContextTokenLearner.ctx's Optional-ness, a defensive assert on
text_projection's actual type (open_clip supports two types there;
forward_ids/forward_embeds only handle one - documented and asserted, not
silently assumed), and a cast + assert for two spots where Ultralytics'
own unannotated code made mypy infer overly-broad unions. Re-verified the
Phase 5 gate check and a real training run after every batch of fixes -
zero regressions.

Also found (only by actually running scripts/run_ablations.py end to end
for the first time) that cbam_worlddetect - ablation (g), "this one is
the paper" - crashed immediately: TGFEMTrainer.get_model() wrongly
required at least one TGFEM layer, but that config deliberately has zero
(CBAM gates instead). Fixed by checking for the WorldDetect head instead,
the actual requirement. All 6 priority ablation variants, the dispatcher's
resume logic, and the cross-variant comparison table are now verified
working end to end at toy scale.

train_tgfem.py + eval_tgfem.py: added speed_ms to results and a matching
column to the comparison table, closing a gap flagged in the last PHASE-7
carried-forward list.

phase-notes/PHASE-6.md, PHASE-7.md, README.md updated to match.
